Block static pointer objects keep their storage and initial zero state,
but their pointed-to array bounds evaluate on each declaration execution.
Both inline calls share the static visit counter and use their own stride.
The final fixture includes inline arrays, +=/-=, prefix updates and &p.
Clang warns that &p cannot be null; this is not a refusal or a value conflict.

